    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d673">

                <pb facs="0775" n="673" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg673"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.119/289: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Italy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-11-28T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                                1919, 2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>2384. With reference to Department’s May 20th, 6 p.m.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d673-f1"/> French Ambassador states his Government is instructing
                    its Embassy at Rome to make representations to Italian Government concerning its
                    attitude on the question of export of arms to China, and asks <pb facs="0776"
                        n="674" xml:id="pg674"/> that you be instructed to join in said
                    representations. In view of Department’s May 20th, 6 p.m. the French Government
                    has been recommended to instruct its Embassy to confer with you in this matter.
                    You may join in proposed representations but it is suggested that before doing
                    so you take into consideration the question whether it would be opportune at the
                    present time for you to renew your representations in this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
